---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Video from '../components/Video.astro';

// ── PROOF ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// The reel below is Vimeo 1214627867, delivered as
// "1.15.26_ChuckWhitehead_Social_Horizontal_Delivered" (47s social cut).
//
// TODO(geoff): confirm two things and I will update the caption:
//   1. Whether the speaker, Chuck Whitehead, may be named. Currently he is
//      not: the credit goes to the organiser who commissioned the work.
// Commissioned by Coldwell Banker Southern Realty (confirmed 2026-07-31).
//
// The archival footage of the talks themselves stays off this site
// permanently: that is the client's asset and the speaker's material, not a
// portfolio piece. Only the reel we produced is ours to show.
//
// SCOPE HONESTY: single-room coverage only. Do not claim concurrent tracks or
// breakout rooms. The offer is the main stage done properly.
// ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
---
<Layout
  title="Corporate Event Video Nashville | SDub Media"
  description="Main-stage conference and corporate event video in Nashville: every talk archived with board audio and your own slides, plus a highlight reel delivered while the event is still fresh."
>
<section>
  <div class="container-narrow text-center">
    <span class="eyebrow">For corporate events</span>
    <h1>Every talk archived.<br>One reel you can actually use.</h1>
    <p style="font-size: 1.1rem; margin-top: 1.5rem;">We cover your main stage: each session recorded end to end for your library, plus a short highlight cut of the day. Audio comes off your board, and your slides go in at full resolution.</p>
    <div style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">
      <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Talk about your event</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section style="background: var(--soft);">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">What you get</span>
      <h2>Two deliverables, not one.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="tiles tiles--two">
      <div class="tile">
        <h3>The Full Archive</h3>
        <p>Every main-stage session recorded start to finish, with the slides cut in. This is the version you put behind a login, send to the people who could not make it, or hand to the speaker. Most organisers find the archive earns its cost the following year, when the content is still working.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tile">
        <h3>The Highlight Reel</h3>
        <p>One short cut of the whole event: the room filling, the speakers, the moments that landed. This is the piece that sells next year's tickets, and it needs to exist while people still remember being there, not six weeks later.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">How we shoot it</span>
      <h2>The details that decide whether it is usable.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="tiles">
      <div class="tile">
        <h3>Audio Off the Board</h3>
        <p>We take a line feed from your AV desk. A keynote captured on a camera microphone in a large hall picks up the room instead of the speaker, and no amount of editing rescues it. If your team has ever been handed conference footage nobody could listen to, this is why.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tile">
        <h3>Your Slides, Not a Filmed Screen</h3>
        <p>Send us the deck and we cut the slides in at full resolution, matched to the moment each one appeared. Pointing a camera at a projection screen is the usual approach and it looks exactly as rough as it sounds.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tile">
        <h3>One Room, Done Right</h3>
        <p>We cover a single room, and we would rather say so than promise four. That means the main stage gets a proper multi-angle setup instead of a scramble between breakouts. If your general sessions are what matter most, this is the trade you want.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section style="background: var(--soft);">
  <div class="container-narrow">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">See it in action</span>
      <h2>The reel from a recent speaker event.</h2>
    </div>
    <Video id="1214627867" title="Highlight reel from a corporate speaker event" />
    <p style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 0.75rem;">Commissioned by Coldwell Banker Southern Realty. Forty-seven seconds, cut for social. The full session was archived separately for their own library.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="container-narrow">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">Why it turns around fast</span>
      <h2>The editing is the part most crews outsource.</h2>
    </div>
    <p>A highlight reel that arrives six weeks after an event has missed its job. Ours do not, because the editing happens on our team rather than in someone else's queue. That is the same reason we can run weekly content for businesses: the edit is never the bottleneck.</p>
    <p style="margin-top: 1.25rem;">We have run this two-output model for years on performance work, where a full-length film goes to the families and a short cut goes on the website. A conference is the same shape in a different room: one long record that has to be complete, one short cut that has to be good.</p>
    <div class="text-center" style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">
      <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Talk about your event</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</Layout>
